\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Portfolio sort approaches illustrated for a single month (December 2024). Each panel plots stock-month observations assigned to \texttt  {r\ .QuartoInlineRender(n\_portfolio)}×\texttt  {r\ .QuartoInlineRender(n\_portfolio)} portfolios based on asset growth rank (x-axis) and size rank (y-axis), both expressed as percentiles. Colors indicate portfolio cell assignment. The univariate sort (left) assigns portfolios on asset growth alone; the independent bivariate sort (center) assigns each dimension independently; the dependent bivariate sort (right) sorts on size first, then on asset growth within size groups.}}{9}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-illustrate-portfolio-helper}{{3}{9}{Portfolio sort approaches illustrated for a single month (December 2024). Each panel plots stock-month observations assigned to \texttt {r\ .QuartoInlineRender(n\_portfolio)}×\texttt {r\ .QuartoInlineRender(n\_portfolio)} portfolios based on asset growth rank (x-axis) and size rank (y-axis), both expressed as percentiles. Colors indicate portfolio cell assignment. The univariate sort (left) assigns portfolios on asset growth alone; the independent bivariate sort (center) assigns each dimension independently; the dependent bivariate sort (right) sorts on size first, then on asset growth within size groups}{figure.caption.10}{}}
